# The browser runtime ships inside the Python package and is served as-is, so
# its bytes are part of what users download and what the size budget measures.
# Pinning LF keeps that measurement identical on Windows, Linux and macOS,
# whatever core.autocrlf a checkout happens to use: with CRLF the same files
# gain a byte per line and the totals drift by several KB without a line of
# code changing.
#
# The icons the stylesheet references ship and are served the same way, so they
# are pinned for the same reason.
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
